<p id="S5.SS1.p13.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p13.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the two horizontal rows are exact.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{c}\in H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(K_{unr}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{c}\in H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(K_{unr}))</annotation></semantics></math> be our unramified Galois cohomology class coming from <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to lift <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to a class in <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the image <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}(\overline{c})\in H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\overline{G}(K_{unr}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}(\overline{c})\in H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\overline{G}(K_{unr}))</annotation></semantics></math>. By the proof of the semisimple case, after maybe replacing <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> with an extension <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K(\pi^{\frac{1}{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K(\pi^{\frac{1}{m}})</annotation></semantics></math> we can lift <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}(\overline{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}(\overline{c})</annotation></semantics></math> to a cohomology class <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}\in H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\overline{G}(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}\in H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\overline{G}(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))</annotation></semantics></math>. We now want to lift <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to a class in <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))</annotation></semantics></math> whose image in <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},G(\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}))</annotation></semantics></math> is the original <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. For this it suffices to show that <math id="S5.SS1.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}(\overline{d})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}(\overline{d})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(f_{1}(\overline{d}))=f_{3}(f_{2}(\overline{c}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(f_{1}(\overline{d}))=f_{3}(f_{2}(\overline{c}))=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it suffices to show that <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is injective. The morphism <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is the direct sum of <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> copies of the morphism <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times})\rightarrow H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},K_{unr}^{\times})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times})\rightarrow H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},K_{unr}^{\times})</annotation></semantics></math> coming from the inclusion of <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{unr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{unr}</annotation></semantics></math>-groups <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times}\hookrightarrow K_{unr}^{\times}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>×</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times}\hookrightarrow K_{unr}^{\times}</annotation></semantics></math>. These groups fit into a short exact sequence</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times}\rightarrow K_{unr}^{\times}\rightarrow\mathbb{Z}\rightarrow 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times}\rightarrow K_{unr}^{\times}\rightarrow\mathbb{Z}\rightarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{unr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{unr}</annotation></semantics></math> acts trivially on <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. We get an exact sequence of abelian groups</span></p>
<table id="S5.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathbb{Z})\rightarrow H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times})\rightarrow H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},K_{unr}^{\times})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>×</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathbb{Z})\rightarrow H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathcal{O}_{K_{unr}}^{\times})\rightarrow H^{2}(\Gamma_{unr},K_{unr}^{\times})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{unr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{unr}</annotation></semantics></math> acts trivially on <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathbb{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathbb{Z})</annotation></semantics></math> is the group of continuous homomorphisms from <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{unr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{unr}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{unr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{unr}</annotation></semantics></math> is profinite, the image of such a homomorphism is finite. Therefore it must be <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is torsion-free. We conclude that <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathbb{Z})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\Gamma_{unr},\mathbb{Z})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence (<a href="#S5.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ 5.1. Completeness of the stack 
          
            
              
                
                Bun
                ρ
              
              
                
                
                  (
                  X
                  ) ‣ 5. Moduli space for the semistable locus ‣ The moduli stack of principal 
      
        ρ
      
    -sheaves and Gieseker-Harder-Narasimhan filtrations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) shows that <math id="S5.SS1.p15.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is injective, as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The argument that allows us to go from semisimple to reductive groups is similar to the argument
of G. Faltings in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fal93</a>, Theorem II.4]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It follows from the argument that <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> can be chosen independently of <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can give a uniform upper bound that depends only on the root data of <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G/Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5.5</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The argument above works verbatim for a general complete discrete valuation ring <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> with perfect residue field <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. mixed characteristic). In that case we can take <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> to be a reductive group over <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> with connected fibers such that the generic fiber <math id="S5.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is residually quasi-split and the analogous conditions (1) and (2) are satisfied.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">In order to construct our generic <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle extension, we will make use of formal gluing, also known as Beauville-Laszlo gluing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx10" title="" class="ltx_ref">BL95</a>]</cite>. Suppose that <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\to\widehat{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\to\widehat{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is a faithfully flat morphism of rings. Let <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in S</annotation></semantics></math> be a nonzero divisor. We denote by <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Glue}_{\text{Aff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Glue</mtext><mtext>Aff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Glue}_{\text{Aff}}</annotation></semantics></math> the category consisting of triples <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{A},A_{f},\varphi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{A},A_{f},\varphi)</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<ol id="S5.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is an affine scheme over <math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Spec(\widehat{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Spec(\widehat{S})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is an affine scheme over <math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Spec(S_{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Spec(S_{f})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism <math id="S5.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:\widehat{A}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}\xrightarrow{\sim}A_{f}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="1.140em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="1.140em">^</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo></mover><msub><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="1.140em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="1.140em">^</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:\widehat{A}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}\xrightarrow{\sim}A_{f}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S5.SS1.p16.2" class="ltx_p">A morphism <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{A},A_{f},\varphi)\to(\widehat{B},B_{f},\psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{A},A_{f},\varphi)\to(\widehat{B},B_{f},\psi)</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a pair of morphisms <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(g_{1}:\widehat{A}\to\widehat{B},\,g_{2}:A_{f}\to B_{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.297em">,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{1}:\widehat{A}\to\widehat{B},\,g_{2}:A_{f}\to B_{f})</annotation></semantics></math> such that their base-changes to <math id="S5.SS1.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})</annotation></semantics></math> fit into a commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S5.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.Ex80.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="94.81" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-41.61px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 222.34 94.81" width="222.34"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,94.81) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(111.17,0) translate(0,41.61)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -111.17 -27.9)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 83.21)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.44)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(44.61,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.66 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.59em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.63em;font-size:10pt;" height="19.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="63.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex80.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\widehat{A}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="1.140em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="1.140em">^</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\widehat{A}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 89.63 0) translate(82.75,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -43.59 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.3em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.63em;font-size:10pt;" height="19.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="73.34"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex80.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A_{f}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="1.140em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="1.140em">^</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces A_{f}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 69.5)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(44.61,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.66 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.59em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.63em;font-size:10pt;" height="19.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="63.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex80.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\widehat{B}|_{\Spec(\widehat{S}_{f})}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="1.140em">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="1.140em">^</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</m